# Agent regression test gates

Run tests yourself at each tier. Do not skip tiers when the change class matches. Prefer **`allTestsParallel`** for full-suite regression (throughput); use **`allTestsSequential`** when parallel would hide the failure class or CI must match.

Reference: `./gradlew printTestSuites`

## Default philosophy

| Goal | Command | Why |
|------|---------|-----|
| Fast iteration | Narrowest task for the change | Red/green loop |
| "Am I done?" full suite | **`allTestsParallel`** | Same coverage as sequential; ~2× faster via IB/emulator BDD shards |
| CI / merge gate | **`allTestsSequential`** | Strict ordering; catches Gradle/E2E sequencing bugs parallel can mask |
| Expert stress | `allTestsParallelStress3` | Only after a parallel flake or before promoting flaky areas |

Do **not** use `allTestsParallelModes` for routine agent work — it parallelizes all four broker modes and may flake.

Add `--rerun-tasks` when verifying a cold run or after Gradle/test infra changes.

## Tier 0 — Trivial change (no test gate)

Typo, comment, README-only, formatting with zero behavior change: no tests required unless the user asks.

## Tier 1 — While implementing (red → green)

Always run the **narrowest** task first; confirm **red for the right reason**, then green after the fix.

| Change touches | Run first |
|------------------|-----------|
| Pure domain (`domain/*`, no broker) | `./gradlew unitTest --tests "<Class>.<method>"` |
| Single unit class | `./gradlew unitTest --tests "daytrader.<pkg>.<Class>"` |
| Programmatic E2E `@E2EEmulatorTest` | `./gradlew e2eEmulatorTests --tests "…"` |
| Programmatic E2E `@E2EIbTest` | `./gradlew e2eIbTests --tests "…"` |
| Programmatic E2E `@E2EPaperTest` | `./gradlew e2ePaperTests --tests "…"` |
| Programmatic E2E `@E2EReplayTest` | `./gradlew e2eReplayTests --tests "…"` |
| Cucumber scenario (stable) | `./gradlew bddIbShardN` / `bddEmulatorShardN` / `bddPaper` / `bddReplay` as appropriate |
| Cucumber `@wip` | `./gradlew bddIbWip` / `bddEmulatorWip` |
| Cross-mode parity | `./gradlew e2eIbTests --tests "E2ECrossModeMarketParityTest"` (and sibling modes if changed) |

If unsure which broker mode: **IB** (`bddIbWip` + `e2eIbTests`) plus emulator when emulator-specific.

## Tier 2 — Before saying a task is done (mode regression)

After the new/changed test passes, run the **affected broker-mode aggregator**:

```bash
./gradlew e2eEmulator   # emulator BDD shards + e2eEmulatorTests
./gradlew e2ePaper
./gradlew e2eIb
./gradlew e2eReplay
```

Run **every mode touched** by the change. If the change is engine/session/broker-adapter shared code, run **all four** mode tasks (still faster than full suite if unit tests already ran separately).

If only domain logic changed with no E2E impact: **`./gradlew unitTest`** is enough at this tier.

## Tier 3 — Full-suite regression (default gate)

Before handing off work on any E2E-sensitive area (see test-first-e2e rule), or when multiple modes/files changed:

```bash
./gradlew allTestsParallel --rerun-tasks
```

This is the **default agent full-suite command** — maximize throughput without `allTestsParallelModes`.

## Tier 4 — Sequential full suite (required in these cases)

Run **`allTestsSequential`** (not parallel) when any of:

- Changed `build.gradle.kts`, `gradle.properties`, E2E task ordering, `mustRunAfter`, sharding, or isolation (`E2EProcessCleanup`, `TestJvmIsolation`, `forkEvery`)
- Tier 3 failed with ordering, timeout, or "passes alone, fails in suite" symptoms
- User explicitly asks for CI-equivalent verification
- Preparing merge / PR summary and parallel suite was not yet green on a cold run

```bash
./gradlew allTestsSequential --rerun-tasks
```

## Tier 5 — Stress (optional)

After stabilizing `@wip` BDD or when hunting flakes:

```bash
./gradlew bddIbStress10          # IB BDD stability
./gradlew e2eIbStress10          # IB mode (bddIb + e2eIbTests)
./gradlew allTestsParallelStress3
```

## Agent checklist (end of task)

1. New/changed test was **red then green** (Tier 1).
2. Affected **`e2e*`** mode task(s) green (Tier 2) if E2E-sensitive.
3. **`allTestsParallel`** green before claiming done (Tier 3), unless change was Tier 0.
4. **`allTestsSequential`** green if Tier 4 triggers applied.
5. Report which commands were run and any tasks skipped (with reason).

Never claim "all tests pass" without running at least the tiers required for the change class.
